*.pyc
.crew/
.hypothesis/
.notify.log
.venv/
__pycache__/
science/warehouse.db
# SQLite's WAL sidecars. They appear whenever the warehouse is read while it is being
# written, which is every run, and committing one would commit a half-applied transaction.
science/warehouse.db-shm
science/warehouse.db-wal

# The dbt half of the same warehouse (crew#74). The .duckdb file is derived from the JSONL
# on disk and rebuilds in seconds. _sources.yml and facts.sql are GENERATED from
# science/sources.json by science/dbt_build.py and are deliberately not committed: a
# committed copy of the registry is a second registry, and the reconcile gate only watches
# the first one.
science/dbt/warehouse.duckdb
science/dbt/models/staging/_sources.yml
science/dbt/models/staging/facts.sql
science/dbt/target/
science/dbt/logs/

# dbt writes this itself on first run. It is a machine-local anonymous-usage id, not
# configuration, and committing it means every machine that clones this fights over it.
science/dbt/.user.yml
science/showcase-state.json
science/ci/
science/foresight-state.json

# The transcript store (crew#319). Rebuilt from ~/.claude/projects by science/transcripts.py,
# every byte read once; delete it to replay from offset zero.
science/transcripts.db
science/transcripts.db-shm
science/transcripts.db-wal
